<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Fraser</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1884–1950</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Fraser was a Scottish-born <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> Labour politician who was prime minister of New Zealand from 1940 to 1949. He led the country through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, built on the welfare state founded under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-joseph-savage">Michael Joseph Savage</a>, and helped draft the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-charter">United Nations Charter</a> in 1945, especially its trusteeship provisions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-fraser.jpg" alt="Peter Fraser" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Office of War Information · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Fraser.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
